<title>JAPAN: Japan does not need extra budget for economy--MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan does not need extra budget for economy--MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan does not need a supplementary budget specifically aimed at stimulating the economy, Vice Finance Minister Tadashi Ogawa told a news conference on Thursday.  </p>
<p>&quot;It is important to add spending on natural disaster preventive measures and other urgently needed projects. But we maintain our view that a supplementary budget aimed at stimulating the economy is not needed,&quot; Ogawa said.</p>
</text>
